                <pb facs="0171" n="63" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg63"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thompson to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Rio
                                de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-10-30"><hi rendition="#italic">October 30, 1893</hi></date>.
                        (Received October 31.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Thompson asks whether he is authorized to protect American merchandise placed
                    on Brazilian barges against the insurgents, using force if necessary. He
                    explains that cargoes can not be landed in Rio de Janeiro unless barges are
                    used.</p>
            </div>
